---

<EventPageLayout
  lang={lang}
  pageKey="presepi-viventi-costiera"
  metaTitle={"Living Nativity Scenes Amalfi Coast 2026/2027: Where and When"}
  metaDescription={"The living nativity scenes of the Amalfi Coast between 26 December 2026 and 6 January 2027: Agerola, Albori di Vietri, Pontone di Scala and Furore. How they work, when they open and how to get there."}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hero={hero}
  schema={schema}
  facts={facts}
  transport={transport}
  slider={slider}
  relatedEvents={relatedEvents}
  cta={cta}
>
  <p slot="intro">A presepe vivente on this coast is not a play: whole villages spend a few evenings going back to the old trades inside their own lanes, with the baker, the blacksmith, the spinner and real livestock. It works because the inland villages have stayed compact and built in stone, and because the whole population takes part.</p>
  <p slot="intro">The four main stagings are at Agerola, in the Campora hamlet, at Albori above Vietri sul Mare, at Pontone in Scala and at Furore. Each has its own evenings, clustered between 26 December and 6 January, and each comune publishes the final calendar in the first weeks of December.</p>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">The four stagings</h3>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">Lattari mountains</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Agerola, Campora hamlet</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">The largest of the four, in a mountain village at 600 metres looking down on the coast. It usually runs on the days just after Christmas and in early January, from late afternoon into the evening.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">Above Vietri</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Albori, Pontone and Furore</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">Albori is a hamlet of Vietri sul Mare listed among the most beautiful villages in Italy, Pontone sits above Amalfi on the climb to Scala, and Furore stages its nativity around the church of San Giacomo. All three run on scattered evenings between late December and Epiphany.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</EventPageLayout>
